CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*invalid implicit conversion from 'const struct exprt' to 'struct resultt'.*$
--
Verifies that `user_defined_conversion_sequence` accepts a converting
constructor of the form `Wrapper(T)` (parameter by value) when the
source is `const T` or `const T&`.  The conversion sequence is
copy-initialization of the parameter from the source via the copy
constructor, then user-defined conversion via the converting
constructor — both legal per [class.copy.ctor]/1 + [dcl.init]/14.
Previously CBMC rejected this because its derived-to-base pointer
path computed `const T*` → `T*` which is not implicit per [conv.qual].
